Cloud Environment Setup & Troubleshooting Journal 🚀

​Executive Summary
​During the setup phase of the AWS Cloud Project Bootcamp, two major infrastructure blockages occurred: a platform transition restriction on Gitpod and an AWS CloudShell account verification hold. This documentation details the root causes and the step-by-step resolution by migrating to GitHub Codespaces and configuring the AWS CLI directly in the cloud container.

​1. Problem Breakdown & Root Causes

​Incident 1: Gitpod Subscription Lockout
​Issue:
Attempting to launch a workspace in Gitpod resulted in a subscription/paywall barrier (rebranded as Ona).
​Root Cause:   Platform model changes removed the previous free tier for cloud workspace creation.
​Impact:       Inability to rely on .gitpod.yml for automated extension installations and workspace provisioning.
​Incident 2: AWS CloudShell Verification Hold

​Issue:   AWS CloudShell returned the error:
Unable to create the environment. Your account verification is in progress...
​Root Cause:    New AWS account security checks temporarily restricted browser-based CloudShell provisioning.
​Impact:     Unable to run aws terminal commands directly within the AWS Management Console UI.
​2. Solution & Resolution Path

​To maintain project momentum without incurring subscription costs or waiting for CloudShell verification:
​Platform Migration: Switched the development environment to GitHub Codespaces (providing free monthly container computing hours).
​Manual Tooling Integration: Installed required extensions (e.g., 42Crunch OpenAPI) directly via the VS Code Extensions Marketplace (Ctrl+Shift+X).
​Direct CLI Installation in Codespaces: Bypassed AWS CloudShell entirely by installing the AWS CLI directly into the Linux container terminal in Codespaces

​3. Step-by-Step Execution Guide

​Step 1: Launch GitHub Codespaces
​Open the GitHub repository.
​Click Code > Codespaces > Create codespace on main.

​Step 2: Install AWS CLI (Linux Terminal Commands)
​Run the following commands sequentially inside the Codespace terminal 

# 1. Download the AWS CLI Linux zip package
curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o "awscliv2.zip"

# 2. Extract the archive
unzip awscliv2.zip

# 3. Run the installer with superuser privileges
sudo ./aws/install

